{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-71934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}15 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-71934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $R$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(R)=5\\cdot 4-10\\cdot 2=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(R)=0,$ we conclude that $R$ is not invertible.\n\n- The matrix $S$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $T$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(T)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $T$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $R$ and $S$ do not have an inverse." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-71934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e145fb97abb632207d6c68caf0fb1c3e75e785931de38c4da626620ab90b1a2"} {"question" "q-71934" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-71934" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$R$ and $S$ only"] ["text" "$R$ and $T$ only"] ["text" "$R$ only"] ["text" "$S$ only"] ["text" "$T$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-71934" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$R$ and $S$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-127826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 15 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-127826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- The matrix $A$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=-3\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 15=-30.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=7\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 4=2.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ does not have an inverse." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-127826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e145fb97abb632207d6c68caf0fb1c3e75e785931de38c4da626620ab90b1a2"} {"question" "q-127826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-127826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $B$ only"] ["text" "$A$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$A$ only"] ["text" "$B$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-127826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-127900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 27 & k\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-127900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =k\\cdot k-27\\cdot 3 \\\\  & ={k}^{2}-81.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2}-81 & =0 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =81 \\\\ k & =\\pm 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $k$ are $k=\\pm 9.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-127900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e145fb97abb632207d6c68caf0fb1c3e75e785931de38c4da626620ab90b1a2"} {"question" "q-127900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-127900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=0"] ["math" "k=\\pm 1"] ["math" "k=\\pm 3"] ["math" "k=\\pm 4"] ["math" "k=\\pm 9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-127900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=\\pm 9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-127903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $M=[\\begin{aligned}t & 5 \\\\ t & 9\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-127903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $M$ is singular if and only if $det(M)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =t\\cdot 9-t\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =9t-5t \\\\  & =4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is $t=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-127903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e145fb97abb632207d6c68caf0fb1c3e75e785931de38c4da626620ab90b1a2"} {"question" "q-127903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-127903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=\\pm 10"] ["math" "k=\\pm 7"] ["math" "t=0"] ["math" "t=4"] ["math" "t=9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-127903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "t=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-316785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 7x-3 & x+8\\end{aligned}]$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-316785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =4\\cdot (x+8)-(-2)\\cdot (7x-3) \\\\  & =4x+32+14x-6 \\\\  & =18x+26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18x+26 & =0 \\\\ 18x & =-26 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{13}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-316785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e145fb97abb632207d6c68caf0fb1c3e75e785931de38c4da626620ab90b1a2"} {"question" "q-316785" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "030bbd667a515bec1f131c0a53fc0f017463c5d414ba3ac8da346fbf04ec0ce2"} {"question" "q-316785" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{13}{9}"] "category" 